<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00002140> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00002140> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-06"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Calcitonin-CTR-Gs/PKA inhibition of osteoclast bone resorption (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "2026-10-05: CALCA hormone activity and CALCR receptor activity placed in adenylate cyclase-activating GPCR signaling pathway (GO:0007189) part of negative regulation of bone resorption; the PLC-activating GPCR pathway (and its negative regulation of ossification parent, left over from the removed S1P arm) was removed from CALCA. Evidence: human osteoclast-like cells, CT-sensitive adenylate cyclase (PMID:11014233, abstract only); human CTR isoforms stimulate cAMP (PMID:7619207, abstract); wild-type human CTR Gs-mediated cAMP with sCT (PMID:28437792, full text); human osteoclasts, CT inhibits resorption and db-cAMP mimics it (PMID:17241109, abstract). Caveat: PMID:11014233 reports that in human osteoclast-like cells PKC activators, not PKA activators, reproduced CT inhibition of resorption."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-05: PKA effectors added from Kajiya et al. 2003 (PMID:12632184, full text, rat resorbing osteoclasts): calcitonin inhibits H+ extrusion by bafilomycin-sensitive V-ATPase and amiloride/EIPA-sensitive NHE (NHE-1 immunostained); mimicked by forskolin/db-cAMP, blocked by H-89/Rp-cAMPs, not PKC- or Ca2+-dependent; transporter protein levels unchanged. Edges PRKACA -causally upstream of, negative effect-> V-ATPase and -> SLC9A1 (mechanism, e.g. direct phosphorylation, not shown). V-ATPase enabler is the GO complex term GO:0033181 (plasma membrane proton-transporting V-type ATPase complex), no subunit specified: the antibody did not identify the a-subunit isoform (ComplexPortal IDs not used; TCIRG1/a3 not added because no experimental complex-membership annotation exists). Role in bone resorption: IMP PMID:31567691 (human TCIRG1-mutant iPSC osteoclasts). V-ATPase MF/location entered as IC (no human direct assay cited). Bone-formation arm: Calcr+/- mice have increased bone formation with normal osteoclast number (Dacquin et al. 2004, PMID:14970190, full text); CT/aCGRP-/- mice have increased bone formation (Hoff et al. 2002, PMID:12488435, abstract only) - consistent with existing ISS (MGI:MGI:101950). Background review: Lerner 2006 J Musculoskelet Neuronal Interact 6:87-95."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-06: Evidence copied from production model gomodel:66b5638000001772 (Signaling by Calcitonin mediated by CALCA/CT ligand activating CALCR receptor (Human)) onto matching edges: PMID:35324283 (CALCA/CALCR enabled by, has input CALCR, has input GNAS, part of AC-activating GPCR signaling), PMID:18057382 (CT in extracellular region), PMID:17110384 (GNAS enabled by, part of AC-activating GPCR signaling), PMID:12135370 (Galphas at plasma membrane; production uses cytoplasmic side of plasma membrane). Not copied: PMID:32296767 (adrenomedullin receptors) and PMID:37963465 (TAAR1) - abstracts do not address CT/CTR; NAS PMID:7588285 (CTR location already IDA); ADCY6 step (PMID:17916776, 23842570) not in this model."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Resorption arm: CALCR directly activates Gs (GNAS; cryo-EM of wild-type human CTR-Galphas-beta1-gamma2, PMID:28437792; adenylate cyclase coupling PMID:1331173), causally upstream of PKA (PRKACA) in negative regulation of bone resorption. PKA requirement: mouse osteoclast-like cells (PMID:8895334), rat osteoclast H+ extrusion (PMID:12632184), human odontoclasts (PMID:14691681), entered as IC because no PKA isoform was identified; PRKACA is a curator assumption. Adenylyl cyclase isoform unknown (GNAS->PKA 'causally upstream of'). Human osteoclast-like cell data (PMID:17535751) used H-7 (PKA+PKC inhibitor), partial block. CTR->Galphaq/11 not modelled (overexpression reconstitution only, PMID:8732687)."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

